<%#
  Public privacy policy. Self-contained on purpose (no layout, inline styles,
  no external assets) so it renders identically whether served at /privacy or
  saved out as a single static .html file -- and so the page itself loads none
  of the analytics, fonts or monitoring scripts it describes.

  Every statement here must stay true to the code:
    * The Google section matches Users::OmniauthCallbacksController and the
      AddGoogleSignInToUsers migration (scopes, stored columns, no tokens kept).
    * The cookie section matches Devise :rememberable (Devise.remember_for),
      config/initializers/warden_hooks.rb, shared/_tracking (Google Analytics)
      and New Relic browser monitoring.
  If any of those change, change this page in the same commit.
  spec/requests/privacy_spec.rb ties several of these together.
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
<title>Privacy Policy &middot; BlueSky &middot; Bluecore Residential</title>
<style>
  /* Light-only on purpose: a dark-themed browser must not render this page
     black-on-black. color-scheme also keeps form controls and scrollbars light. */
  :root { color-scheme: light; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 16px 72px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
    color: #212529;
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
  header.masthead {
    margin: 0 -16px 40px;
    padding: 26px 16px;
    background-color: #005089;
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  header.masthead .inner { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
  header.masthead .product { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; }
  header.masthead .org { font-size: 13px; opacity: .85; margin-top: 2px; }
  h1 { font-size: 28px; line-height: 1.25; margin: 0 0 6px; }
  h2 {
    font-size: 19px;
    margin: 40px 0 10px;
    padding-top: 18px;
    border-top: 1px solid #e3e6ea;
  }
  h3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 24px 0 6px; }
  p, li { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  ul { padding-left: 22px; }
  .effective { color: #6c757d; font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  a { color: #005089; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; margin: 12px 0 20px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 15px; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #dfe3e8; padding: 8px 10px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background-color: #f4f6f8; font-weight: 600; }
  .callout {
    background-color: #f2f7fb;
    border-left: 4px solid #005089;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }
  .no-store { background-color: #f3faf5; border-left: 4px solid #1e7c43; padding: 14px 16px; margin: 20px 0; }
  .callout p:last-child, .no-store p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  footer.pagefoot { margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid #e3e6ea; color: #6c757d; font-size: 14px; }
  code { background-color: #f4f6f8; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 14px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="masthead">
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="product">BLUESKY</div>
    <div class="org">Bluecore Residential</div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap">

  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="effective">Effective 14 October 2026. Applies to the BlueSky web application at www.blue-sky.app.</p>

  <p>
    BlueSky is a private, internal lead-management and leasing application operated by Bluecore
    Residential. It is not a consumer product and is not open to public sign-up. Every BlueSky
    account is created by a BlueSky administrator.
  </p>

  <p>
    This policy explains what personal information BlueSky collects about the people who use it
    &mdash; Bluecore Residential staff, and anyone else an administrator has given an account &mdash;
    why, and what we do with it.
  </p>

  <p>
    BlueSky is also used to manage enquiries from prospective and current residents. Information
    about those people is processed on Bluecore Residential's behalf and is not described by this
    policy; questions about it should be directed to Bluecore Residential.
  </p>

  <h2>Signing in with Google</h2>

  <p>
    BlueSky offers &ldquo;Sign in with Google&rdquo; as its main way to sign in. Using it is not
    required: signing in with an email address and password remains available.
  </p>

  <h3>What we ask Google for</h3>
  <p>
    We request two standard, non-sensitive permissions: your <strong>email address</strong> and your
    <strong>basic profile</strong> (<code>email</code> and <code>profile</code>). We do not request
    access to Gmail, Drive, Calendar, Contacts, photos, or any other Google service, and we cannot
    read them. We ask Google for access only while you are signing in, not for ongoing access.
  </p>

  <h3>What Google sends us, and what we keep</h3>
  <p>When you sign in, Google sends BlueSky a small profile record. We keep only part of it:</p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Sent by Google</th><th>Do we store it?</th><th>What it is used for</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Email address</td>
        <td><strong>Yes</strong></td>
        <td>Matching you to your existing BlueSky account.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Whether that email address is verified</td>
        <td>No &mdash; checked, not stored</td>
        <td>We refuse the sign-in unless Google confirms the address is verified.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Google account identifier</td>
        <td><strong>Yes</strong></td>
        <td>Tying your BlueSky account to one specific Google account, so a different Google account cannot later claim your email address.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>First and last name</td>
        <td><strong>Yes</strong></td>
        <td>Keeping the name shown in BlueSky current.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Profile picture</td>
        <td>No</td>
        <td>Not used. Profile pictures in BlueSky are uploaded separately.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Language and organisation details</td>
        <td>No</td>
        <td>Not used.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Because Google has verified that you control your email address, a successful Google sign-in
    also completes your account's email confirmation if it was still pending, and lifts a temporary
    lock caused by repeated incorrect passwords.
  </p>

  <div class="no-store">
    <p>
      <strong>We do not store Google access tokens or refresh tokens.</strong> They are used once,
      during sign-in, and then discarded. BlueSky therefore has no standing access to your Google
      account and cannot read anything from it between sign-ins.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    BlueSky's use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services
    User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Signing in with Google never creates an account.</strong> If the Google address you use
      does not already match a BlueSky account, you are refused and told to contact an administrator.
      Google sign-in is a way to open a door you already have a key to &mdash; it is not a way in.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h3>Disconnecting Google</h3>
  <p>
    To remove the link between your BlueSky account and your Google account, ask a BlueSky
    administrator to unlink it. The stored Google account identifier, the Google email address, and
    our record of the name Google last sent are deleted at that point; the name shown on your BlueSky
    profile stays as it is. You can also revoke BlueSky's access from your Google account directly at
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Other information BlueSky holds about you</h2>

  <p>Whether or not you use Google sign-in, BlueSky stores:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account details</strong> entered by you or an administrator &mdash; name, email address,
      role, time zone, the properties and teams you are assigned to, and optionally phone numbers, an
      email signature, a Slack handle, notes, a profile picture, and your notification preferences.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sign-in records</strong> &mdash; the number of times you have signed in, the dates and
      times of your current and previous sign-in, the <strong>IP addresses</strong> used, and failed
      password attempts. We keep these to protect accounts and investigate misuse.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your work in BlueSky</strong> &mdash; the leads assigned to you, the notes, tasks and
      messages you create, and a change history recording who changed a record, when, and from which
      IP address. These are attributed to you and visible to other BlueSky users according to their
      permissions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Pages you visit in BlueSky.</strong> While you are signed in, BlueSky records which of
      its pages you open and the page you came from, against your account, so we can see how the
      application is used.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A password</strong>, stored only as a salted cryptographic hash, if you use password
      sign-in. We cannot recover or read your password.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Cookies and similar technologies</h3>
  <p>BlueSky uses these cookies and browser storage:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>A session cookie</strong>, set whenever you use BlueSky. It is strictly necessary for the
      application to work, and it is deleted when you close your browser.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Two sign-in cookies</strong>, set when you sign in, holding an encrypted copy of your
      account identifier and a timestamp. They are cleared when you sign out and deleted when you
      close your browser.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A &ldquo;Remember me&rdquo; cookie</strong>, set only if you tick &ldquo;Remember
      me&rdquo; when signing in with a password. It keeps you signed in across browser restarts for up
      to two weeks, and signing out invalidates it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics cookies</strong> (<code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&hellip;</code>), set
      by Google Analytics on BlueSky's pages, including the sign-in page, to count visits and
      understand how the application is used. They last up to two years unless you clear them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Performance-monitoring storage</strong>: our application-monitoring service stores a
      session identifier in your browser's local storage to measure page load times and catch errors.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The first three are set by BlueSky itself and exist only to keep you signed in. There are no
    advertising cookies.
  </p>

  <h3>Analytics and other scripts on BlueSky's pages</h3>
  <p>
    BlueSky's pages load Google Analytics, which receives the pages you view, your browser and device
    details, your IP address (from which Google derives an approximate location), and the name of the
    property you have selected in BlueSky. They also load an application-monitoring script that
    reports page performance and errors, web fonts from Google's font service, and a
    browser-compatibility notice from browser-update.org; each of these receives your IP address and
    browser details when your browser fetches it. This privacy page loads none of them.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use this information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To authenticate you and keep you signed in.</li>
    <li>To decide what you are allowed to see and do, based on your role and property assignments.</li>
    <li>To attribute your work and changes within the application.</li>
    <li>To send you account email &mdash; account confirmation, password resets, unlock instructions &mdash; and task notifications.</li>
    <li>To keep the application secure, investigate misuse, and diagnose faults.</li>
    <li>To understand how the application is used, so we can improve it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not use this information for advertising, we do not sell it, and we do not use it to build
    profiles for any purpose beyond operating BlueSky.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>
    Other BlueSky users at Bluecore Residential can see your name, contact details, role and property
    assignments, and your work in the application, subject to their own permissions.
  </p>
  <p>
    Beyond that, we share personal information only with the service providers that run BlueSky on
    our behalf, and only to the extent needed to run it: our cloud hosting provider and its database,
    caching and log-management services; our file-storage provider (for uploaded profile pictures);
    the services that deliver BlueSky's email and text messages, including messages you send to
    prospects through BlueSky; our application-monitoring and error-alerting services, including the
    workplace messaging service that error alerts are posted to; and Google, for sign-in, analytics
    and web fonts. We do not sell personal information or disclose it for anyone else's marketing. We
    may also disclose information where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your account and its associated records for as long as your account exists. When someone
    leaves, their account is normally deactivated rather than deleted, so that historical records stay
    attributable and reports remain accurate. Google Analytics keeps the data it collects for the
    retention period set in our Google Analytics account. To request deletion, use the contact below.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    BlueSky is served over HTTPS and requires an account to access. Passwords are stored only as
    salted hashes, and an account is temporarily locked after repeated incorrect passwords. Access is
    limited by role and by property assignment, and administrators can deactivate an account
    immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Sign in with a password instead of Google.</strong> Use &ldquo;Sign in with an email
      address and password instead&rdquo; on the sign-in page. If you have never set a password, use
      &ldquo;Forgot your password?&rdquo; there to set one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Revoke access at Google.</strong> You can remove BlueSky's access at any time from your
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account permissions</a> page. Because
      we hold no Google tokens, this takes effect immediately.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Access, correct, or delete your information.</strong> Contact your BlueSky administrator.
      Some records must be kept for security or legal reasons.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change what we collect or how we use it, we will update this page and the date at the top
    of it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>BlueSky is operated by Bluecore Residential.</p>
  <p>
    Because every account is created by an administrator, questions about this policy or about your
    information are best raised with your BlueSky administrator, who can also unlink your Google
    account or deactivate your access on request.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top: 32px;">
    <a href="/users/sign_in">&larr; Back to sign in</a>
  </p>

  <footer class="pagefoot">
    BlueSky is an internal application of Bluecore Residential and is not available to the general public.
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
